course: dictionary
lesson: 15876
title: Unified: joined into one
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unified means joined together to make one whole. Think of separate puzzle pieces clicked into one picture. «The separate villages became one unified country.» Villages that have joined into one country are unified.
explain: Unified can also mean made the same or working in a consistent way everywhere. «The school uses unified rules in every classroom.» Every classroom follows the same rules, so the rules are unified. Unify is the verb, and unified is its past form, so it shows that something has already been joined or made the same.
explain: Check the clues. In «The players trained together and played as one unified team», the words together and as one show that the players are joined, not working alone. Swap in joined together for unified and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Unified means joined together into one whole.
fact: Unified can also mean made the same or consistent everywhere.
fact: Unify is the verb, and unified is its past form.
fact: «A unified country» is one country made from smaller parts.
fact: «Unified rules» are the same rules everywhere.
exercise: «The separate villages became one unified country.» What does unified mean here? | Painted in bright colours | Split into many small pieces | Very small in size | *Joined together into one whole
exercise: «The school uses unified rules in every classroom.» What does unified suggest? | *The same rules everywhere | Rules that change every day | Each class makes up its own rules | No rules at all
exercise: Unified comes from a verb. Find and copy that verb. | separate | country | *unify | village
test: «The players trained together and played as one unified team.» What does unified mean in this sentence? | *Joined together, working as one | Split into smaller teams | Very tired after the match | Lost and confused
test: Which word is the past form of unify? | Unity | Unifying | Unifies | *Unified
exam: Which phrase best means unified? | Painted blue | *Joined together, the same everywhere | Scattered and mixed up | Broken into pieces
